Description: R package built from the JASA reproducibility supplement of Niu, Ni, Pati and
    Mallick (2024) <doi:10.1080/01621459.2023.2233744>, "Covariate-Assisted Bayesian Graph
    Learning for Heterogeneous Data". The PxG model partitions samples with a truncated
    Dirichlet process whose allocation is informed jointly by a response matrix and a
    covariate matrix, and fits a sparse Gaussian graphical model within each cluster.
    Two specifications are provided exactly as in the supplement: a Gaussian / G-Wishart
    sampler in R for small graphs ('PxG_GW') and a pseudo-likelihood spike-and-slab
    neighbourhood-selection sampler in C++ for larger graphs ('PxG_PL'), together with the
    covariate-only and graph-only comparison models, the TCGA breast cancer data analysed in
    the paper, the authors' saved intermediate results, the comparison methods of the paper
    compiled from the same supplement (BM13 via 'LSGraph', JRNS, k-lasso) or wrapped (mSSL),
    and scripts and vignettes that reproduce every figure and number in the paper from the
    packaged functions.
